WEBVTT

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.717
A hundred-year war, all because

00:00:22.761 --> 00:00:25.155
a computer tricked us
into fighting each other.

00:00:25.198 --> 00:00:26.765
It's so embarrassing.

00:00:26.808 --> 00:00:29.376
A lot of civilizations blame it
on the supernatural.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.335
At least
you didn't fall for that.

00:00:31.378 --> 00:00:32.423
Yeah.

00:00:32.466 --> 00:00:34.251
That would have been crazy.

00:00:36.166 --> 00:00:38.385
Here's your "lord" AGIMUS,
safely disconnected

00:00:38.429 --> 00:00:40.257
from his network of drones.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.782
&lt;i&gt;Hey, now, this has all been
a huge mistake.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:46.524
just let me access your computer
mainframe,

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.091
&lt;i&gt;and I'll explain everything.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:48.134 --> 00:00:49.875
Nice try.
Save it for the roboticists

00:00:49.918 --> 00:00:52.007
at the Daystrom Institute.
Ransom?

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.314
All right, fella, in you go.

00:00:54.358 --> 00:00:56.490
&lt;i&gt;So, you're the muscle, huh?&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:59.928
&lt;i&gt;Bet you couldn't throw me into
that control console over there.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:59.972 --> 00:01:01.713
Over there?
By that network port?

00:01:01.756 --> 00:01:03.149
That's nothing.
I could easily toss...

00:01:03.193 --> 00:01:05.978
Oh. Oh, you almost got me.

00:01:06.021 --> 00:01:08.676
&lt;i&gt;I underestimated
your intelligence.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.288
&lt;i&gt;-Clearly,
you should be the captain...
- Yeah.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:11.331 --> 00:01:12.332
Anyone hungry?

00:01:12.376 --> 00:01:13.986
I could eat.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.033
Ugh. I don't know why I keep

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:19.861
giving alien street food
a chance.

00:01:19.905 --> 00:01:21.515
It's always such a gamble.

00:01:21.559 --> 00:01:23.300
Captain, we're being hailed.

00:01:23.343 --> 00:01:26.172
On screen.
Queen Paolana.

00:01:26.216 --> 00:01:29.219
To what do we owe
this pleasure... again?

00:01:29.262 --> 00:01:32.396
&lt;i&gt;We're having a spot of engine
trouble here on theMonaveen.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:32.439 --> 00:01:35.138
&lt;i&gt;My royal engineers can't seem
to suss out the hiccup.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:35.181 --> 00:01:37.052
- Uh-huh. &lt;i&gt;
- Carol, you're the closest&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:38.706
&lt;i&gt;Starfleet ship in the quadrant.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.144
&lt;i&gt;As such,
I must call upon the aid&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:41.187 --> 00:01:42.449
&lt;i&gt;of your chief engineer.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:42.493 --> 00:01:44.190
What a surprise.

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:45.887
- Captain, we have completed
the... &lt;i&gt;
Ah!&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:45.931 --> 00:01:48.803
&lt;i&gt;My dear Andarithio!
Have you been eating?&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:48.847 --> 00:01:50.327
&lt;i&gt;You're wasting away.
And what happened&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.980
&lt;i&gt;-to that mustache?
It is thinning.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:52.024 --> 00:01:53.068
- Hello, Mother. &lt;i&gt;
- Are you taking your vitamins?&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.331
&lt;i&gt;You must start eating eggs.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:08.579 --> 00:03:11.712
Boimy's got a phaser rifle.
Nice.

00:03:11.756 --> 00:03:14.106
Now, how are those different
from regular phasers?

00:03:14.149 --> 00:03:15.716
Uh, they take two hands.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.936
You're just jealous 'cause
you pulled a boring cargo trip

00:03:17.979 --> 00:03:19.285
to the Daystrom Institute

00:03:19.329 --> 00:03:21.505
while I get
to wrangle giant centipedes.

00:03:21.548 --> 00:03:23.681
Ooh. You're on the mission
to Dansk?

00:03:23.724 --> 00:03:26.553
Yup. Another class M
for my planetary review log.

00:03:26.597 --> 00:03:29.687
How are you excited for giant,
nightmarish centipedes?

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.036
You know, back on the &lt;i&gt;Titan,&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:32.385
we did this kind
of wet work all the time.

00:03:32.429 --> 00:03:34.605
Ugh. Don't say "wet work."
Gross.

00:03:34.648 --> 00:03:36.824
What? It was work, it was wet.
It-it-it was fine.

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:39.044
I'm just glad Ransom's finally
taking my experience to heart.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:43.135
"Ensign Boimler,
report for reassignment

00:03:43.178 --> 00:03:45.746
to escort of cargo
to the Daystrom Institute"?

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:47.313
But that's what you're doing.

00:03:47.357 --> 00:03:49.489
Aw, sorry, man. No getting eaten
by an arthropod today.

00:03:49.533 --> 00:03:50.838
Instead you can load the crates.

00:03:50.882 --> 00:03:52.405
And, hey,
I'm gonna do you a favor.

00:03:52.449 --> 00:03:53.841
We'll spray 'em down. You can
still have your wet work.

00:03:53.885 --> 00:03:55.887
Aw.

00:04:06.332 --> 00:04:09.030
&lt;i&gt;Okay, team.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:09.074 --> 00:04:10.336
Listen up.
Some of you might have heard

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:11.946
that my mother's back
on the ship.

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:13.339
Now, we all know the score.

00:04:13.383 --> 00:04:15.776
Please don't fall
for one of her deceptions.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.169
Uh, wait. What deceptions?

00:04:17.212 --> 00:04:19.476
Mother is the queen of Hysperia,
my homeworld.

00:04:19.519 --> 00:04:20.868
When I joined Starfleet,

00:04:20.912 --> 00:04:23.436
I abdicated my birthright
as prince.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.047
Hysperia... Oh! That's
the planet with the dragons

00:04:26.091 --> 00:04:28.049
that got colonized
by all those Ren faire types.

00:04:28.093 --> 00:04:29.573
Did you grow up in a castle?

00:04:29.616 --> 00:04:33.316
Yes, but a life of
mythical adventure can't compare

00:04:33.359 --> 00:04:35.318
to working
on the old impulse engine.

00:04:35.361 --> 00:04:38.059
Which is exactly why
my mom is always trying

00:04:38.103 --> 00:04:39.496
to trick me into having sex.

00:04:39.539 --> 00:04:40.714
Uh, sorry. What now?

00:04:40.758 --> 00:04:43.717
By Hysperian law,
if I lose my virginity,

00:04:43.761 --> 00:04:46.111
then I automatically
become king.

00:04:46.154 --> 00:04:49.419
I'd have to resign from
Starfleet and take the throne.

00:04:52.683 --> 00:04:56.164
Here he is, Your Majesty.

00:04:56.208 --> 00:04:57.731
Mother, if you're planning
on tricking me

00:04:57.775 --> 00:04:59.342
into intercourse, think again.

00:04:59.385 --> 00:05:01.344
The only lady I love
is two decks tall

00:05:01.387 --> 00:05:03.258
and pumped full of dilithium.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:07.175
My sweet Andarithio,
I promise, no tricks this time.

00:05:07.219 --> 00:05:08.481
- Really?
- Yes.

00:05:08.525 --> 00:05:10.178
Obviously, I still hope one day

00:05:10.222 --> 00:05:11.876
you'll give up this nonsense,
but I see now

00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:13.704
that I was pushing you away.

00:05:13.747 --> 00:05:15.619
Oh. So, then why are you here?

00:05:15.662 --> 00:05:18.578
The dragonbreath engines in our
ships have been breaking down.

00:05:18.622 --> 00:05:20.014
We have no idea why.

00:05:20.058 --> 00:05:22.365
Hysperia will be left
defenseless.

00:05:22.408 --> 00:05:24.889
My son, I'm asking you
to help your people,

00:05:24.932 --> 00:05:27.500
not as a prince, but as...

00:05:27.544 --> 00:05:29.502
...an engineer.

00:05:29.546 --> 00:05:32.200
Okay, now that I can do.

00:05:32.244 --> 00:05:34.681
Mr. Rutherford,
you're with me.

00:05:34.725 --> 00:05:38.163
It's time to prove to my mother
that I'm more than a royal stud.

00:05:38.206 --> 00:05:41.384
Billups! Billups! Billups!

00:05:41.427 --> 00:05:44.387
&lt;i&gt;Aw, man, I'm not
cut out for this.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:45.866
But you fix the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos
all the time.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.738
Yeah, but this is different.
We're talking about

00:05:47.781 --> 00:05:49.783
a fancy cruiser
stuffed with puffy monarchs.

00:05:49.827 --> 00:05:52.177
I-I'm gonna go tell Billups
he should use someone else.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.614
No! You belong there
as much as anyone else.

00:05:54.658 --> 00:05:56.094
You need to get outside
your comfort zone.

00:05:56.137 --> 00:05:58.270
But I love my zone.
It's so comfortable.

00:05:58.313 --> 00:06:01.969
So you'll really turn down
working on a whole new engine?

00:06:02.013 --> 00:06:03.971
Uh, well, it would be nice

00:06:04.015 --> 00:06:06.321
to see how the other half
channels their antimatter.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:08.236
That's the ticket.
Just ignore all the fancy gowns,

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.542
and make sure not
to say anything rude,

00:06:09.586 --> 00:06:11.109
be careful how you stand.
Oh, and you should

00:06:11.152 --> 00:06:12.676
- definitely learn how to curtsy.

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:16.462
- Ah...
- Hey, cheer up.

00:06:16.506 --> 00:06:18.159
This is a blessing in disguise.

00:06:18.203 --> 00:06:20.248
You really wanted to be covered
in centipedes right now?

00:06:20.292 --> 00:06:21.946
It would've looked great
on my evaluations.

00:06:21.989 --> 00:06:24.122
- Yeah, assuming you survived.
- What was that?

00:06:24.165 --> 00:06:25.515
Oh, just kick back, man,
enjoy the trip.

00:06:25.558 --> 00:06:26.777
After we drop this thing off,

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.344
we'll grab
some Okinawa ramen and...

00:06:31.259 --> 00:06:32.217
Whoa. Uh, sensors say

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.827
&lt;i&gt;we hit a gravimetric shear.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:33.871 --> 00:06:36.003
&lt;i&gt;Oh, no.
We're in the gravity well.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:36.047 --> 00:06:38.310
Uh, try manual controls.
Auto is out.

00:06:38.353 --> 00:06:39.442
Ugh!

00:06:42.662 --> 00:06:44.534
No response! Brace for impact!

00:07:01.855 --> 00:07:03.248
Mariner? Mariner?

00:07:03.291 --> 00:07:05.555
I'm okay. It's just a fracture.

00:07:05.598 --> 00:07:07.557
- Ugh. Just?

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:09.254
Oh, God, I can't even
look at it.

00:07:09.297 --> 00:07:11.735
Well, good news.
It's a breathable atmosphere,

00:07:11.778 --> 00:07:14.520
wherever we are.

00:07:16.391 --> 00:07:19.090
Looks like we aren't the only
ones to hit that anomaly.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:23.224
Most systems are down,
no way to send a distress call.

00:07:23.268 --> 00:07:24.704
No. We-we were outside
of communication range.

00:07:24.748 --> 00:07:26.837
It's gonna be a week
before anyone even notices

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.229
that we haven't checked in.

00:07:28.273 --> 00:07:29.709
Good thing
the replicator's still intact.

00:07:29.753 --> 00:07:32.451
Computer, iced tea,
splash of lemonade, cold.

00:07:32.495 --> 00:07:34.801
&lt;i&gt;Black licorice, dry.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:34.845 --> 00:07:36.499
Great.

00:07:36.542 --> 00:07:38.544
The least nutritious food that
tastes the most like poison.

00:07:38.588 --> 00:07:40.241
&lt;i&gt;Help. Help me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:40.285 --> 00:07:41.634
Did you hear something?

00:07:41.678 --> 00:07:43.636
&lt;i&gt;Ah, thank you, friend.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.116
&lt;i&gt;I am freed.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:45.159 --> 00:07:46.552
Aw, crap.
It's the evil computer.

00:07:46.596 --> 00:07:48.075
We're not supposed
to interact with it.

00:07:48.119 --> 00:07:49.729
&lt;i&gt;- Hey, hey!&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:49.773 --> 00:07:51.252
&lt;i&gt;Before you close that,
consider...&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:51.296 --> 00:07:52.558
- Dang it. &lt;i&gt;
- I can contact help!&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:52.602 --> 00:07:55.648
-[grunts, sighs] &lt;i&gt;
- Oh, come on, friends.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:55.692 --> 00:07:57.476
&lt;i&gt;Help me help you.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:01.828 --> 00:08:05.440
Hysperian culture can be
a bit, uh, distracting.

00:08:05.484 --> 00:08:08.139
Whoa.

00:08:09.923 --> 00:08:12.404
Wow. Sir, is that you?

00:08:20.978 --> 00:08:23.023
Prince Andarithio!

00:08:23.067 --> 00:08:24.416
Just call me Billups.
Thank you.

00:08:24.459 --> 00:08:25.809
It's such an honor
to bask in your glory.

00:08:25.852 --> 00:08:27.332
Our beloved Prince Andarithio
has returned.

00:08:27.375 --> 00:08:28.463
Ah, okay,
don't-don't need the necklace.

00:08:28.507 --> 00:08:29.987
- Huzzah! Huzzah!
- Thank you.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:32.598
Uh, but you don't have to bask.
Uh, not really a prince.

00:08:34.818 --> 00:08:38.430
My chief blacksmith is simply
baffled by the loss of power,

00:08:38.473 --> 00:08:39.997
so I don't know what you can do.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.477
Rutherford, check the levels
of the dragonsblood flame.

00:08:42.521 --> 00:08:44.001
- The what?
- Sorry.

00:08:44.044 --> 00:08:45.568
The primary fusion reactor.

00:08:45.611 --> 00:08:49.354
Hysperians renamed everything
to sound like magic.

00:08:49.397 --> 00:08:52.226
Uh, the, uh, elf matrix
seems like it's...

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:53.619
- Don't do that.
- Sorry.

00:08:53.663 --> 00:08:55.752
The subspace field matrix
should be online.

00:08:55.795 --> 00:08:57.318
It's not? That's impossible.

00:08:57.362 --> 00:08:59.146
The plasma levels would be
completely unregulated.

00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:00.713
Son, are you saying

00:09:00.757 --> 00:09:03.324
the problem is beyond
your engineering acumen?

00:09:03.368 --> 00:09:05.283
No. No. Okay, no.
We will just have

00:09:05.326 --> 00:09:07.154
to run a full diagnostic
from the bottom up.

00:09:07.198 --> 00:09:10.114
You can run
your full diagnostic

00:09:10.157 --> 00:09:11.811
along my bottom up, my liege.

00:09:11.855 --> 00:09:13.073
- Nope, thank you.

00:09:13.117 --> 00:09:15.336
Ignore them
and just get to work.

00:09:24.128 --> 00:09:25.738
&lt;i&gt;Friend, I'm worried about you.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:25.782 --> 00:09:27.958
&lt;i&gt;Your hair-- patchy,
your skin-- pimply.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:28.001 --> 00:09:29.742
&lt;i&gt;-Are you sick?&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:29.786 --> 00:09:31.744
Boims, don't engage.
That's how they get you.

00:09:31.788 --> 00:09:33.746
- Evil computers are so chatty. &lt;i&gt;
- Tell you what.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:36.053
&lt;i&gt;Just connect me
to an engineering conduit.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:36.096 --> 00:09:39.534
&lt;i&gt;I could whip up a sonic shower.
Wouldn't that feel splendid?&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:39.578 --> 00:09:42.407
- Uh, what was that?

00:09:45.323 --> 00:09:47.717
Can it see us?
- I don't know. Just don't move.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.458
&lt;i&gt;I know when I'm feeling scared,
the best thing you can do&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:50.502 --> 00:09:52.678
&lt;i&gt;is get plugged
into a shuttlecraft computer.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:52.722 --> 00:09:54.158
Will you stop it?

00:09:54.201 --> 00:09:56.334
- Uh...

00:09:57.552 --> 00:09:59.424
Uh...

00:10:01.731 --> 00:10:03.297
Crap. The food.

00:10:03.341 --> 00:10:05.691
Oh, no, no, no. It's going
to town on the rations.

00:10:05.735 --> 00:10:07.650
Stupid AGIMUS.
Now we got nothing to eat.

00:10:07.693 --> 00:10:09.303
&lt;i&gt;It's fine.
My scans indicate&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:09.347 --> 00:10:10.696
&lt;i&gt;you could lose
a couple pounds anyway.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.785
Excuse me?!
Oh, you're gonna go there?

00:10:12.829 --> 00:10:14.134
Mariner, don't engage. Remember?

00:10:19.705 --> 00:10:21.141
Hey, get out of my PADD.

00:10:21.185 --> 00:10:23.143
&lt;i&gt;Sorry. Just stretching.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:23.187 --> 00:10:24.623
You get the door,
I'll watch him.

00:10:24.667 --> 00:10:26.625
Hey. Now keep your cords
to yourself, or I'll have

00:10:26.669 --> 00:10:28.496
a hard time remembering
which regulation keeps me

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:29.976
from kicking you to pieces.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.412
&lt;i&gt;Okay, I'm sorry.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:31.456 --> 00:10:34.111
&lt;i&gt;I wouldn't want
to cause any trouble.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:43.207 --> 00:10:46.253
Computer, water, please.

00:10:46.297 --> 00:10:48.255
&lt;i&gt;Black licorice. Black.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:49.604 --> 00:10:51.389
&lt;i&gt;I could fix that.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:51.432 --> 00:10:53.870
&lt;i&gt;Tap water, still,
bubbly with lime.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:53.913 --> 00:10:55.349
&lt;i&gt;Just plug me in.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:55.393 --> 00:10:57.177
- Shut up!

00:10:57.221 --> 00:10:59.745
- Mariner, we kind of do
have to find water soon.
- I know, yeah.

00:10:59.789 --> 00:11:02.008
We know there's life here, which
means there's got to be water.

00:11:02.052 --> 00:11:03.357
- Right? &lt;i&gt;
Tell you what.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:03.401 --> 00:11:04.968
&lt;i&gt;You two go look for it,&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:05.011 --> 00:11:06.752
&lt;i&gt;and I'll stay here
and guard the computer.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:06.796 --> 00:11:08.928
&lt;i&gt;Just set me down there,
right in front of it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:08.972 --> 00:11:10.451
- I'll just strap him up.
- Wait.

00:11:10.495 --> 00:11:11.844
Why bring him with?
We could just, like,

00:11:11.888 --> 00:11:13.237
bury him, like Data's head.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.326
Okay, actually,
Data's head was in a cave.

00:11:15.369 --> 00:11:17.241
And it's our duty
to respect sentient life.

00:11:17.284 --> 00:11:18.764
He's a manipulative
supercomputer

00:11:18.808 --> 00:11:19.896
who controlled a planet.

00:11:19.939 --> 00:11:21.506
And we're Starfleet.

00:11:21.549 --> 00:11:24.596
Oh, stupid Starfleet ethics.

00:11:25.423 --> 00:11:28.731
&lt;i&gt;No! Come on, leave me be!&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:40.612 --> 00:11:43.571
Edible. I think
I can climb up and reach it.

00:11:43.615 --> 00:11:45.748
- You have a broken arm.
- It's fractured.

00:11:45.791 --> 00:11:48.272
I still have a better shot at it
than Mr. Falls-Out-of-His-Bunk.

00:11:48.315 --> 00:11:50.143
That barely happens anymore.

00:11:50.187 --> 00:11:51.536
And plus, I'll have you know,

00:11:51.579 --> 00:11:53.233
I took up rock climbing
on the &lt;i&gt;Titan.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:53.277 --> 00:11:56.236
I swear, if you bring up your
study abroad one more time...

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.935
You're just mad because
I'm finally catching up to you

00:11:58.978 --> 00:12:01.894
in my planetary
exploration skills.

00:12:01.938 --> 00:12:04.897
- Ooh, so close.

00:12:04.941 --> 00:12:06.812
You know, if that was a rock
wall, you would have had it.

00:12:06.856 --> 00:12:09.206
Oh, just shut it!

00:12:09.249 --> 00:12:11.425
- Ah, I can drink that.
- Oh, my God, random liquid.

00:12:11.469 --> 00:12:13.079
- Gimme, gimme, gimme, gimme!

00:12:13.123 --> 00:12:14.907
It tastes
like black licorice, too?!

00:12:14.951 --> 00:12:16.779
Are you kidding me?!

00:12:16.822 --> 00:12:18.345
Well, I don't see
a better option.

00:12:18.389 --> 00:12:20.783
Do you?!

00:12:20.826 --> 00:12:22.219
No.

00:12:24.656 --> 00:12:27.746
&lt;i&gt;Well, you know, I could have
fixed your replicator.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:31.010
&lt;i&gt;Right now you could have been
enjoying a cheeseburger&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:31.054 --> 00:12:33.056
&lt;i&gt;or blueberry muffins or...&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:33.099 --> 00:12:34.405
Don't.

00:12:34.448 --> 00:12:36.668
&lt;i&gt;...guacamole.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:36.711 --> 00:12:38.017
&lt;i&gt;I have rights!&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:42.065 --> 00:12:44.415
&lt;i&gt;Help! Starfleet!
I'm under attack!&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:44.458 --> 00:12:45.808
Uh...

00:12:45.851 --> 00:12:47.940
&lt;i&gt;-Help! Help! Help!
- Crabs.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:47.984 --> 00:12:50.900
Get out of here.
Get out of here. Get, get.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.512
&lt;i&gt;Well done, Bradward. My thanks.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:54.555 --> 00:12:57.254
How about you stop mentioning
food, and we'll be even, okay?

00:12:57.297 --> 00:12:58.690
&lt;i&gt;I can do you one better.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:58.733 --> 00:13:01.475
&lt;i&gt;Your partner is not
what she seems.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:01.519 --> 00:13:02.825
Yeah, I've heard the rumors.

00:13:02.868 --> 00:13:04.696
&lt;i&gt;I accessed
your ship's memory bank.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:04.739 --> 00:13:06.306
&lt;i&gt;Don't you wonder why&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:09.527
&lt;i&gt;your commander took you off
the Dansk mission?&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:11.050
&lt;i&gt;-Yo, Jack, do me a solid.
- Huh?&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:11.094 --> 00:13:12.835
&lt;i&gt;Throw Boimler
on that escort mission with me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:12.878 --> 00:13:14.358
&lt;i&gt;He doesn't want
to wrangle centipedes?&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:14.401 --> 00:13:15.968
&lt;i&gt;No. He's not ready for Dansk.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:16.012 --> 00:13:17.622
&lt;i&gt;Okay?
What does a centipede have?&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:17.665 --> 00:13:19.754
&lt;i&gt;Pincers and poison mandibles.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:19.798 --> 00:13:21.756
&lt;i&gt;Yeah, you wouldn't want
the guy getting pincered.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.193
&lt;i&gt;He wouldn't react well.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:23.236 --> 00:13:24.890
&lt;i&gt;All right, I'll reassign him.
Bummer.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:24.934 --> 00:13:27.023
&lt;i&gt;I thought
he was ready for this.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:30.896 --> 00:13:32.985
Oh. What's going on?
Are we still stranded?

00:13:33.029 --> 00:13:34.813
You pulled me off
the Dansk mission?!

00:13:34.857 --> 00:13:36.815
What?
Did that thing tell you that?

00:13:36.859 --> 00:13:38.512
Oh, you mean the truth?

00:13:38.556 --> 00:13:40.732
It's clearly trying to get us
to fight. You know that, right?

00:13:40.775 --> 00:13:42.734
Now Ransom thinks I'm not
cut out for the big stuff!

00:13:42.777 --> 00:13:45.215
You're not!
Well, at-at least not yet.

00:13:45.258 --> 00:13:46.912
I was just looking out for you.

00:13:46.956 --> 00:13:49.219
I'm sure
that my &lt;i&gt;Titan&lt;/i&gt; experience...

00:13:49.262 --> 00:13:51.308
Enough with the &lt;i&gt;Titan!&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:51.351 --> 00:13:53.005
This trip is just
proving me right.

00:13:53.049 --> 00:13:55.399
You can't even handle mind games
from a hundred-year-old router.

00:13:55.442 --> 00:13:59.403
&lt;i&gt;Rude. Aah! Help me, Bradward!
Where is she taking me?&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:59.446 --> 00:14:01.187
Mariner, drop the computer.

00:14:01.231 --> 00:14:04.799
Nope. You are on time-out until
you stop siding with the enemy.

00:14:10.283 --> 00:14:13.765
Wow, sir. You're recalibrating
those plasma injectors

00:14:13.808 --> 00:14:15.941
faster than I've ever seen.

00:14:15.985 --> 00:14:17.247
Hmm.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:18.901
I got it.

00:14:19.727 --> 00:14:21.251
Aha! Faulty resonators.

00:14:21.294 --> 00:14:23.209
They've probably been degrading
all over the fleet

00:14:23.253 --> 00:14:24.994
because, you know, resonance.

00:14:25.037 --> 00:14:27.648
Weird. That should've come up
in our initial scan.

00:14:27.692 --> 00:14:29.824
The royal navy is saved.

00:14:29.868 --> 00:14:31.870
Let's hear it
for Prince Andarithio

00:14:31.914 --> 00:14:33.698
and his calloused squire.

00:14:33.741 --> 00:14:35.961
Huzzah! Huzzah! Huzzah!

00:14:36.005 --> 00:14:38.833
I have to admit, I'm impressed.

00:14:38.877 --> 00:14:41.445
Seeing you in your element
finally makes me understand

00:14:41.488 --> 00:14:43.186
why you love this Starfleet.

00:14:43.229 --> 00:14:46.493
One could say I'm even...
Oh, what's the word?

00:14:46.537 --> 00:14:48.843
- Proud?
- I'll only be proud
once you take my place

00:14:48.887 --> 00:14:52.543
on the throne,
but today I'm satisfied.

00:14:52.586 --> 00:14:55.633
&lt;i&gt;Lieutenant Billups,
report to my ready room.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:55.676 --> 00:14:57.243
On my way, Captain.

00:14:57.287 --> 00:15:00.290
Finish up here, and I'll be
right back, and, hey, nice work.

00:15:00.333 --> 00:15:02.248
Thank you, sir.

00:15:04.598 --> 00:15:06.557
You needed me, Captain?

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:09.125
No, not really.
I was just giving you an out

00:15:09.168 --> 00:15:11.779
in case your mother was up
to her usual antics.

00:15:11.823 --> 00:15:14.086
Actually, it's been great.
I-I think she respects me.

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.870
I mean,
she really just wanted me

00:15:15.914 --> 00:15:17.002
to diagnose her engine problem.

00:15:17.046 --> 00:15:18.525
As a mother, I can understand

00:15:18.569 --> 00:15:20.179
that she wants
what's best for you.

00:15:20.223 --> 00:15:22.529
Well, that's always been
the problem, but today

00:15:22.573 --> 00:15:24.705
I might have finally
earned her respect.

00:15:26.098 --> 00:15:27.317
What?

00:15:29.754 --> 00:15:31.799
No.

00:15:31.843 --> 00:15:35.542
Oh, Your Majesty,
what hath happened?

00:15:35.586 --> 00:15:38.893
Uh, I don't know.
All readings were nominal.

00:15:38.937 --> 00:15:40.634
Long live the queen.

00:15:40.678 --> 00:15:42.549
The queen is dead.

00:15:47.424 --> 00:15:49.992
Ensign Tendi, there was
an accident on the &lt;i&gt;Monaveen.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:50.035 --> 00:15:53.125
Oh, no. I can prep
for triage, and...

00:15:54.474 --> 00:15:55.867
Rutherford?!

00:16:14.799 --> 00:16:18.324
&lt;i&gt;Scans indicate...
this ship's engines are intact!&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:18.368 --> 00:16:19.891
This could be our ticket
out of here.

00:16:19.934 --> 00:16:21.762
&lt;i&gt;Plug me into that port.
I can release the doors.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:21.806 --> 00:16:24.069
Yeah, right. No,
we'll try that ship over there.

00:16:24.113 --> 00:16:25.940
Why? AGIMUS can get us
into this one. It's right here.

00:16:25.984 --> 00:16:28.160
&lt;i&gt;He's right, Mariner.
Come on! I can help.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:28.204 --> 00:16:30.380
Oh, my God, Boimler,
since the minute we crashed,

00:16:30.423 --> 00:16:32.730
he's been trying to get
his danglies into a computer.

00:16:32.773 --> 00:16:34.166
No, uh-uh. No, no way.

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:35.646
I thought a maverick
like you would do anything

00:16:35.689 --> 00:16:36.734
to get out of here.

00:16:36.777 --> 00:16:38.257
Anything that isn't stupid.

00:16:39.693 --> 00:16:41.130
Give him to me.

00:16:41.173 --> 00:16:43.915
Ugh. This is exactly why
I got you reassigned.

00:16:43.958 --> 00:16:45.656
You are just a naive little...

00:16:47.092 --> 00:16:48.963
What are you doing?
Get the hell off me!

00:16:49.007 --> 00:16:50.226
I'm sick
of you bossing me around

00:16:50.269 --> 00:16:51.488
like you're better than me!

00:16:51.531 --> 00:16:52.706
You had no right
to get me reassigned!

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:56.014
&lt;i&gt;-Yes. Yes!&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:57.668 --> 00:16:59.278
Stop! Don't make me do this.

00:16:59.322 --> 00:17:02.107
Oh, please. Like you would
ever have the guts to...

00:17:05.197 --> 00:17:06.329
&lt;i&gt;You had no choice.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:06.372 --> 00:17:08.026
&lt;i&gt;-She lacks your vision.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:09.680
&lt;i&gt;Now quick, to the ship!&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:24.999
Come.

00:17:25.043 --> 00:17:28.090
Andy, I'm so sorry.
If there's anything I can do.

00:17:28.133 --> 00:17:32.137
Captain, I... I'm afraid
I must resign from Starfleet.

00:17:32.181 --> 00:17:34.096
Resign?
What are you talking about?

00:17:34.139 --> 00:17:35.967
I was trying
to prove something today,

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:38.491
and all I did
was get people killed.

00:17:38.535 --> 00:17:40.928
It wasn't your fault. You can't
blame yourself for the...

00:17:40.972 --> 00:17:42.495
The Hysperian throne is vacant.

00:17:42.539 --> 00:17:44.976
My people need a leader.
They need a king.

00:17:45.019 --> 00:17:48.762
And I must perform
the Royal Copulation.

00:17:48.806 --> 00:17:52.418
I don't have the luxury of being
your chief engineer anymore.

00:17:52.462 --> 00:17:54.246
Are you sure
you want to do this?

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:56.770
No. I &lt;i&gt;have&lt;/i&gt; to do this.

00:17:56.814 --> 00:17:58.990
- Ooh, yes.
- Uh.

00:17:59.033 --> 00:18:01.123
Good luck, Your Majesty.

00:18:01.166 --> 00:18:03.690
Oh, w-will it hurt?

00:18:07.694 --> 00:18:10.828
Rutherford, I... I can't.

00:18:10.871 --> 00:18:12.656
This isn't happening.

00:18:12.699 --> 00:18:15.180
Computer,
locate Ensign Rutherford.

00:18:15.224 --> 00:18:19.576
&lt;i&gt;Cybernetic implant
of Ensign Rutherford is located&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:19.619 --> 00:18:22.709
&lt;i&gt;in Section 8
of the Hysperian shipMonaveen.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:22.753 --> 00:18:24.189
His implant
is still transmitting.

00:18:24.233 --> 00:18:26.757
A little part of him
is still alive.

00:18:28.498 --> 00:18:30.152
Ugh!

00:18:32.197 --> 00:18:34.460
Boimler, you idiot.

00:18:42.512 --> 00:18:43.948
You sure
this thing can still fly?

00:18:43.991 --> 00:18:45.558
- Seems pretty beat-up. &lt;i&gt;
Yes.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:45.602 --> 00:18:48.431
&lt;i&gt;Yes, I can bring it on line.
I just need access.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:48.474 --> 00:18:51.129
Okay, I'll sub you in
as the navigation controls.

00:18:51.173 --> 00:18:53.653
Aw, shoot, the access port's
locked behind this panel.

00:18:53.697 --> 00:18:55.873
We would need an auxiliary
power source to open it.

00:18:55.916 --> 00:18:58.528
&lt;i&gt;Oh, please.
Here. Use my battery.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:05.361 --> 00:19:06.927
&lt;i&gt;Oh, yes. Yes, yes, yes, yes.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:06.971 --> 00:19:10.148
Yes!

00:19:10.192 --> 00:19:11.976
Oh, Rutherford,

00:19:12.019 --> 00:19:13.804
if I hadn't told you to get out
of your comfort zone,

00:19:13.847 --> 00:19:16.633
you'd still be alive
and comfortable.

00:19:24.118 --> 00:19:26.208
- Rutherford?!
- Hey, Tendi!

00:19:26.251 --> 00:19:27.774
You here for the feast?

00:19:27.818 --> 00:19:29.689
- You're alive!

00:19:29.733 --> 00:19:31.474
Huh? Of course I'm alive.

00:19:31.517 --> 00:19:33.084
Well, what about the explosion?

00:19:33.127 --> 00:19:35.217
Wait. What explosion?
The queen transported me here

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:38.002
for the celebration feast
because I did such a good job.

00:19:38.045 --> 00:19:42.006
Raise a glass
to King Andarithio,

00:19:42.049 --> 00:19:46.663
who at this very moment
is destroying his virginity!

00:19:46.706 --> 00:19:48.839
What?! No!
Billups loves his virginity.

00:19:48.882 --> 00:19:50.580
I mean,
he loves being an engineer!

00:19:50.623 --> 00:19:52.016
He doesn't want to be a king.

00:19:52.059 --> 00:19:53.322
I don't care what he wants.

00:19:53.365 --> 00:19:54.758
He shouldn't be wasting his life
twiddling around

00:19:54.801 --> 00:19:56.238
on a dinky spaceship.

00:19:56.281 --> 00:19:57.804
It was all a scam!

00:19:57.848 --> 00:19:59.371
We've got to warn Billups!

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.246
Blocking comms?!

00:20:04.289 --> 00:20:07.161
I've got to
stop Billups from doing the do!

00:20:07.205 --> 00:20:08.728
You're too late.

00:20:08.772 --> 00:20:12.297
My royal guards are trained
from birth to skip foreplay.

00:20:18.782 --> 00:20:20.349
Ooh.

00:20:26.093 --> 00:20:28.705
Your 'stache is so regal.

00:20:31.098 --> 00:20:32.709
- Out of my way, horse!

00:20:35.277 --> 00:20:37.279
Billups!

00:20:40.325 --> 00:20:42.501
Huh? Where's Billups?

00:20:42.545 --> 00:20:43.894
Did his kingdom come?

00:20:43.937 --> 00:20:45.504
Bathroom.

00:20:45.548 --> 00:20:47.027
Come on. Come on.

00:20:47.071 --> 00:20:48.855
You got this. You're a king.

00:20:48.899 --> 00:20:50.292
Ensign?

00:20:50.335 --> 00:20:52.032
Sir, I'm alive!
It was one of your mom's tricks.

00:20:52.076 --> 00:20:54.339
- You don't have to do sex!
- What?

00:20:54.383 --> 00:20:57.342
- Was I too late?
- No! I needed more time
to warm up!

00:20:57.386 --> 00:20:59.866
- This prince remains dry!
- Yeah!

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:01.999
Yes!
All right!

00:21:02.782 --> 00:21:04.044
Boimler, no!

00:21:04.088 --> 00:21:05.829
&lt;i&gt;You are too late!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:05.872 --> 00:21:07.831
&lt;i&gt;AGIMUS reigns!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:07.874 --> 00:21:09.485
&lt;i&gt;With this ship's materials,&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:09.528 --> 00:21:12.792
&lt;i&gt;I will produce a whole fleet
of murder drones!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:12.836 --> 00:21:18.711
&lt;i&gt;This planet-- nay, this system--
will be mine!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:18.755 --> 00:21:21.714
&lt;i&gt;You fool! You trusted me!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:21.758 --> 00:21:23.368
Nah, I used you.

00:21:23.412 --> 00:21:25.544
&lt;i&gt;What?&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:25.588 --> 00:21:28.155
Uh, I've been using your power
cell to send a distress signal.

00:21:28.199 --> 00:21:30.723
You were too busy scheming
to notice. You've been Boim'ed.

00:21:30.767 --> 00:21:32.595
&lt;i&gt;But-but no!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:32.638 --> 00:21:35.032
&lt;i&gt;You plugged me
into the navigation console!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:35.075 --> 00:21:36.990
&lt;i&gt;I control this ship!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:37.034 --> 00:21:40.385
Buddy, we're not even
near the nav console.

00:21:40.429 --> 00:21:42.387
All you control is
the dimmer switch.

00:21:42.431 --> 00:21:43.910
&lt;i&gt;But I... I...&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:43.954 --> 00:21:45.651
Boims! What? No.
I totally thought

00:21:45.695 --> 00:21:47.653
you were siding with this thing.

00:21:47.697 --> 00:21:49.481
Yeah, sorry I lied
and stunned you.

00:21:49.525 --> 00:21:52.310
I just needed him to trust me so
he'd let me access his battery.

00:21:52.354 --> 00:21:53.355
Aw, look at you.

00:21:53.398 --> 00:21:55.400
Who's the evil computer now,
huh?

00:21:55.444 --> 00:21:57.750
&lt;i&gt;You dare mock AGIMUS?!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:57.794 --> 00:22:00.797
&lt;i&gt;I shall... I shall blind you!&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:03.887 --> 00:22:07.020
&lt;i&gt;Faking your death,
blowing up your own ship?&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:07.064 --> 00:22:10.067
This is a new low, Mother.

00:22:10.110 --> 00:22:12.678
A meager price to pay
to get you on the throne.

00:22:12.722 --> 00:22:14.506
I love Starfleet.

00:22:14.550 --> 00:22:16.508
Okay, and I don't want
to live in a castle

00:22:16.552 --> 00:22:19.119
with pet dragons
and all the mutton I can eat.

00:22:19.163 --> 00:22:20.512
You need to accept the fact

00:22:20.556 --> 00:22:23.994
that I'll be a virgin
for the rest of my life.

00:22:24.037 --> 00:22:27.214
Well, we'll see about that.

00:22:27.258 --> 00:22:30.522
Billups! Billups! Billups!

00:22:30.566 --> 00:22:33.307
I'm sorry I pushed you
to go work on the &lt;i&gt;Monaveen.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:33.351 --> 00:22:34.396
I'm as bad as the queen.

00:22:34.439 --> 00:22:35.701
You should work
wherever you want.

00:22:35.745 --> 00:22:37.050
If that means staying
in engineering

00:22:37.094 --> 00:22:38.661
here on the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,
then great.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:38.704 --> 00:22:40.053
Are you kidding? I loved it!

00:22:40.097 --> 00:22:42.012
I got to work
on an expensive engine,

00:22:42.055 --> 00:22:44.101
eat a feast and save my boss.

00:22:44.144 --> 00:22:46.451
I even got "blown up."

00:22:46.495 --> 00:22:49.454
Yeah, I-I guess
there's just gonna be times

00:22:49.498 --> 00:22:51.804
every now and then when it seems
like you've died, huh?

00:22:51.848 --> 00:22:54.241
Ha. That's Starfleet.
But you can handle that, right?

00:22:54.285 --> 00:22:56.287
- Oh, yeah, I'm fine.

00:22:56.330 --> 00:22:59.116
No biggie.

00:23:01.118 --> 00:23:03.816
&lt;i&gt;Well, this has been quite
an adventure.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:03.860 --> 00:23:05.688
&lt;i&gt;You two have shown me&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:05.731 --> 00:23:09.256
&lt;i&gt;that trust and friendship
are better than manipulation.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:11.476
&lt;i&gt;I'm ready to try being good
for a change.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:13.086
&lt;i&gt;- There.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:16.133
&lt;i&gt;I just deleted all
my manipulative subroutines.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:16.176 --> 00:23:18.788
&lt;i&gt;I want to be
a Starfleet officer like you!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:18.831 --> 00:23:20.920
&lt;i&gt;Just drop me off at the Academy.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:20.964 --> 00:23:24.141
&lt;i&gt;I can be the next Seven of Nine.
AGIMUS of One!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:24.184 --> 00:23:25.534
&lt;i&gt;You'll regret this!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:25.577 --> 00:23:27.710
&lt;i&gt;I will conquer this lab,&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:27.753 --> 00:23:30.016
&lt;i&gt;and then I will
take over the Federation!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:31.627
&lt;i&gt;I will destroy you all!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:33.455
&lt;i&gt;You'll do nothing of the sort,&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:33.498 --> 00:23:35.718
&lt;i&gt;for I am going
to annihilate the Federation!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:35.761 --> 00:23:37.284
&lt;i&gt;Tremble at my power!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:37.328 --> 00:23:39.461
&lt;i&gt;With that programming?
Good luck.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:39.504 --> 00:23:42.115
&lt;i&gt;You should self-destruct,
if you even can.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:42.159 --> 00:23:43.987
&lt;i&gt;You both suck!&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:44.030 --> 00:23:46.946
&lt;i&gt;You don't understand what being
an evil computer even is!&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:49.095 --> 00:24:49.531
Chirp.
